        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "reflection",
          "order",
          "line of symmetry"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A mirror line shows reflection. A shape with a line of symmetry matches its mirror image.\nRotational symmetry means a shape looks the same after turning less than a full turn. A square has rotational symmetry of order 4 and a rectangle has order 2.\nSome shapes have both kinds. An equilateral triangle has 3 lines of symmetry and rotational order 3."
        }
